senses.gloss:
stūpa, m.
(1) (rarely nt.; = Pali thūpa, AMg. thūbha, rarely thūva; Skt. Lex., in lit. only Buddh. and Jain), relic-mound, tope: Mvy 〔6999〕; SP 〔239.1 ff.〕; Mv 〔ii.287.3〕; 〔363.16〕; Av 〔i.119.7〕; ˚pa-bimbāni Kv 〔13.11〕; 〔36.19〕; ˚pabhedanam Mvy 〔2334〕, one of the upānantarīya, q.v.; ˚pa-bhedaka Kv 〔94.23〕; common everywhere; as nt., stūpaṃ kāritaṃ (n. sg.) Mv 〔i.61.1〕;
(2) (Pali, see next but one) turret or pinnacle of a building, in prākāraparikhādvāra-stūpābhinigūḍhaḥ Av 〔ii.115.8〕, see Speyerʼs note.
